Z||000001||btoth||03-28-2001||09:48 AM||||Have you tried reinstalling PIP?  Sometimes when you uninstall or install new programs under windows they overwrite .dll files or other system files and screw up everything.  I'd try reinstalling it if you haven't already and see if that clears up any problems you're having.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RNGCRSH||03-28-2001||11:29 AM||||I have not used PIP, but if your pics are stored at a geocities/yahoo page and PIP links to that page, then It wont work anymore due to a policy change blocking external picture linking.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||03-30-2001||03:55 AM||||My7, I think the sig you were posting was the one I made for you. If so, it is possible that you had been posting the sig file I had stored on my server.........I cleaned up the server recently to make some room for needed space and that file may have been deleted. If so, and you have it on your computer, just upload it using PIP and set your signature file to reflect the new server/file name and it will post everytime you want it to.........usually (in Internet Explorer) the indication of the red X indicates that an image called for is not found on the server (meaning it has either not been uploaded or it can't find that particular file)||||reg||1
